// CONFORMANCE-CASE
// spec: 21-standard-library-semantics
// facility: rule.stdlib.x509 [Cert-Parse] [Verify-Chain] [Host-Match] (D-0160); conf.x509-refusals
// kind: positive
// expect: ok
// expect-stdout-hex: 
//
// A test PKI made with openssl (stress/crypto/pki/gen.sh): a root with an
// EC P-384 key, an intermediate with an RSA key (path length 0) that signs
// with RSA-PSS, a leaf with an EC P-256 key for test.example,
// *.wild.example and 127.0.0.1, and a leaf valid for one day. Checked at a
// fixed time, 2030-06-01: another host, an expired leaf, a time before
// validity, a missing intermediate and an empty trust store are each
// refused with their reason; a truncated certificate does not parse.

